.TH STATUS 8 "November 2026" "TeraStation TS5800D" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
status \- display physical bay map, RAID volume status, and SMART disk health
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B status
[\fB\-a\fR | \fB\-d\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B status
is a read-only diagnostic utility for the Buffalo TeraStation TS5800D running Debian 12.
It maps physical chassis bays (Bay 1..8) to Linux block devices and reports real-time
MDADM RAID health or extended SMART diagnostics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Display physical bay mapping, disk status, and MDADM RAID volumes
.RI ( /dev/md0 ,
.IR /dev/md1 ,
.IR /dev/md2 ).
This is the default mode when no option is provided.
.TP
.B \-d
Display detailed SMART disk health per bay using
.BR smartctl (8)
(power-on hours, reallocated sectors, pending sectors, uncorrectable errors, and temperature).
Automatically elevates with
.BR sudo (8)
when invoked as a non-root user.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show brief usage summary and exit.
.SH STATUS VALUES (\-d)
.TP
.B HEALTHY
SMART self-assessment passed with no pending sectors and low/zero wear.
.TP
.B WATCH
SMART passed and zero pending sectors, but historical reallocated sectors (>= 20)
or reported uncorrectable errors (>= 10) warrant periodic observation.
.TP
.B FAILED
SMART self-assessment failed or pending sectors (> 0) detected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rebuild (8),
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR mdadm (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Marcelo Santos \- ActionSys
